{
  // Dead-component detection (2026-08-08 issue-pattern audit, measure P4.4).
  //
  // WHAT THIS CLOSES. `tsc` is perfectly happy with an exported React component
  // that nothing imports, and ESLint never looks across files — so a vertical
  // slice can ship complete and be reachable from no route at all. That is
  // cluster K of the audit: #818, #786, #606, #578, #438, "implementiert, aber
  // inert". Nothing in this repository measured it.
  //
  // `.jsonc`, not `.json`, purely so this can be written down where it applies.
  "$schema": "https://unpkg.com/knip@6/schema.json",

  // ── What is reported ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
  //
  // Only unused FILES and unused EXPORTS. Measured 2026-08-08 with the full
  // default set: 9 unused files, 38 unused exports, 26 unused exported types
  // — 73 findings, too many to be a useful signal in one screen, and the third
  // group is not the defect this is for. `src/api/types.ts` is a hand-kept
  // mirror of the backend's OpenAPI surface; a response type the UI does not
  // read yet is the file doing its job, not dead code. Dropping it leaves 47.
  //
  // Worked down to **zero** on 2026-08-16 (#1207). All nine files were genuinely
  // superseded, each by a live successor — the Karenz card by
  // DiagnosisResultsPanel, the water-mix summary by NutrientCalculationsPage,
  // the phase stepper by three separate timelines, the location list by
  // LocationTreeSection, the plant-count step by the per-species counts in
  // PlantSelectionStep. None was a wiring defect, which is worth recording
  // because the issue that opened this predicted one and was wrong.
  //
  // The largest single item was not on the file list at all: FertilizerGanttChart
  // lost its call site in the #347 split of NutrientPlanDetailPage (2026-07-04)
  // and survived six weeks as 1 699 lines whose only remaining consumer imported
  // one interface from it. A file can be almost entirely dead and still look
  // alive to a file-level check.
  //
  // Dependency, binary and unlisted-import checks are off for the same reason:
  // npm-audit, npm-licenses and the bundle budget already watch that surface,
  // and a second opinion on it would only add noise to a lane whose one
  // question is "is this UI reachable?".
  "include": ["files", "exports"],

  // ── Scope ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  //
  // `public/` is deliberately outside `project`: runtime-config.js and sw.js
  // are served by nginx and referenced from index.html at runtime, so a static
  // importer graph cannot see them and would report both as dead every run.
  "project": ["src/**/*.{ts,tsx}", "scripts/*.mjs"],

  // Entry points beyond what knip's Vite/Vitest plugins already detect. The
  // detected ones (src/main.tsx via index.html, the vitest setup file, the
  // config files) are NOT restated here: a restated default drifts silently
  // when the tool's detection changes, and knip reports it as redundant.
  "entry": ["src/**/*.test.{ts,tsx}"],

  // An export used only inside its own file is a private helper that happens to
  // carry the keyword — worth tidying, not worth a CI lane.
  "ignoreExportsUsedInFile": true,

  // The KAMI illustration barrel is an asset catalogue, not code. Its entries
  // are `export { default as … } from './x.svg'` re-exports of files the KAMI
  // media pipeline produces ahead of the surfaces that will show them, so an
  // entry with no importer is inventory, not debt — and Vite tree-shakes it, so
  // it costs nothing in the bundle. Eighteen phase and state motifs are in that
  // position today.
  //
  // Exempted by path rather than by a blanket ignore list, so the exemption says
  // what it covers and stops covering anything else.
  "ignore": ["src/assets/brand/illustrations/index.ts"]

  // ── NO BASELINE, DELIBERATELY ─────────────────────────────────────────
  //
  // The 47 findings were NOT suppressed here. An ignore list would have made
  // this lane green on day one and measured only future regressions — while the
  // nine unreachable files it named were precisely the debt the audit asked
  // for. They were worked down instead (#1207), which is what the plan below
  // always said had to happen first.
  //
  // The lane stays advisory for now (see the `deadcode` job in
  // .github/workflows/frontend.yml). It is green as of 2026-08-16, but a check
  // is promoted on measured history per NFR-018 §4, not on the day it first
  // passes: one green run says nothing about its false-positive rate on real
  // changes. Promote it when the history supports it — not by editing this
  // comment.
}
